# Pairs with GuardCoversFence. A new activation's recovery reads and re-stamps
# TAIL, so its provider instance holds a current view of it, but it re-seeds the
# allocator from the trim tail and the calls in motion it can see, not from the
# TAIL it read: after a move to another silo it claims offsets at or below
# batches its predecessor committed.
MODULE: GuardCoversFenceRecoveryIgnoresTail
TARGET: GuardCoversFence
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: recovery refreshes the fence but re-seeds below the TAIL it read
PERTURBS: ShardRecover

--- FIND
    /\ resyncing = "recover"
    /\ next' = ReseedNext
--- REPLACE
    /\ resyncing = "recover"
\* MUTATION: the re-seed ignores the TAIL it read.
    /\ next' = Max({tail} \cup {o + 1 : o \in orphans \ hidden})
--- END
--- FIND
WithCrossSiloMove == FALSE
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: raises the bound so a lost activation may move to another silo.
WithCrossSiloMove == TRUE
--- END
